  },
  {
    "episode_id": 91897,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91897.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and that's Dick Morris said something to me once upon a time that stuck with me. He said, Republicans have their couch potatoes too. It's funny. You don't think about it, but there are lots of people out there that just don't vote for whatever reason. So, you know, it's Republicans are going to get better at spending time going out and finding those people. I know Democrats typically have an easier time with it because you can find them concentrated on college campuses or maybe urban city districts. But, you know, hopefully you're able to find those Republicans that would be inclined to vote, but just don't, in kind of a Republican, but just don't show up on Election Day. Is that possible?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Dick Morris made a statement to me once.",
