    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91897.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, to disclose it to you, like I've formally endorsed President Trump. I'm with him. And that's no disrespect to our governor. I think our governor is great. But, you know, elections are choices and I've made mine. And the reason why is very simple. One, I think from a foreign policy standpoint, we got to have somebody who can step in day one and kind of get the world back in order. For all the talk from the Democrats, Obama was going to start World War III. If Donald Trump became president, the opposite happened. The world was safer. You know, global order was in a better place. You know, with this guy currently in the White House, we have, you know, we have proxy wars in Ukraine and all kind of other craziness going on. And so that's the reason for me. But when it comes to this indictment, this thing is a complete travesty of justice. And just to surmise, the president of the united states any president of the united states we know they take classified documents we know they take other documents and other effects with them Every president does this. It's not new stuff. What they're trying to do is say that, oh, because he talked about a document with somebody else, allegedly, I might add, because the audio hasn't been released. This audio, this transcript is a leaked transcript with, by which, by the way, is illegal, and it's leaked to the press. Some put that aside for a moment. They're basically saying that because he did that, and because of that, and because he moved boxes, he obstructed justice. That is the stupid thing I've ever heard in my life. Obstructing justice means there has to be an underlying crime, and there is no underlying crime, because presidents are allowed to have documents. They all have documents. Well, this is a political hit job, and I think that people are sick of it, not just Republicans, but I think people are sick of it. Because if you look at our cities, where you have district attorneys who are not enforcing the law, but then they're going to go and invent charges against a former president simply because you just don't like the man. And let's be very clear. A lot of this is we don't like them. That actually is un-American. It is destructive of our judicial system. And I think that's the stuff that we got to stand against as Americans.",
